# Line endings for GENERATED files only.
#
# Several --check stages compare a generated file byte-for-byte against a fresh run. Git's
# default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so those files come
# out of a Windows clone with different bytes from the ones the generator writes — and every
# one of them is reported stale with nothing changed. Pinning them to LF fixes that at source.
#
# Deliberately NOT repo-wide. 105 tracked files are stored with CRLF, almost all of them
# PowerShell-generated tenant exports under docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/contracts/deployed/ and
# docs/reference/foundational/. Those are evidence, recorded verbatim; a blanket rule would
# renormalise all of them and change the bytes of the record.

docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/registers/flow-list-map.json            text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/FLOW_CATALOGUE.md             text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/registers/endpoint-workflow-ids.json    text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/registers/portal-endpoint-workflow-ids.json text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/registers/flow-trigger-auth.json        text eol=lf
docs/reference/process-inventory.json        text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/registers/http-flow-registry-spec.json  text eol=lf
docs/deployment/EXECUTION_RUNBOOK.md         text eol=lf
docs/folio-Master-Flows-and-Endpoints/deployment/internal/dynamic-operations.json text eol=lf
docs/visual/platform-data.js                 text eol=lf

# DGO Correspondence Mailer: generated flow definitions are held byte-for-byte by
# `npm run test:mailer`; the zips are binary and must never be touched by EOL conversion.
mailer/flows/definitions/*.json              text eol=lf
mailer/flows/flows.catalogue.json            text eol=lf
mailer/flows/packages/*.zip                  binary
releases/*.zip                               binary
